            <ArticleTitle>Discoid Lupus Erythematosus on a Pre-exi Patch of Chronic Radiodermatitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>266-267</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A middle,aged male had lesions of discoid lupus erythematosus developing within a patch of chronic radio-dermatitis on the side of the neck. Radio-dermatitis developed at the site of X-ray irradiation received 35 year ago for tuberculosis of the cervical lymph glands. Subsequently, he had developed 3 other lesions of DLE on the upper back.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
